<div class="article-title">
X-Men Join Avengers: Doomsday? Wolverine, Deadpool and the Multiverse Mystery Explained
</div>

<div class="meta">
Updated November 8, 2026 · Marvel · X-Men · Avengers: Doomsday · MCU
</div>


<!-- MAIN OFFICIAL CYCLOPS IMAGE -->

<img
class="hero-image"
src="https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/images/g_disneymovies_avengers_doomsday_6_adf215ee.jpeg?region=0%2C0%2C1300%2C730"
alt="James Marsden as Cyclops in Marvel Studios Avengers Doomsday"
loading="eager"
fetchpriority="high"
onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/images/g_disneymovies_avengers_doomsday_4_99d2c6b0.jpeg?region=0%2C0%2C1300%2C730';"
>

<div class="image-caption">
Cyclops and the returning X-Men characters in Marvel's Avengers: Doomsday. Image: Disney / Marvel Studios.
</div>


<div class="notice">

<strong>MARVEL UPDATE:</strong>

The original X-Men movie universe is returning in Avengers: Doomsday. Disney's official cast announcement includes several familiar X-Men actors, bringing a new generation of Marvel characters into the multiverse story.

But could this be the beginning of something even bigger? Fans are asking whether Wolverine, Deadpool and even Tobey Maguire's Spider-Man could become part of the same extraordinary crossover.

</div>


<article>

<p>
For years, Marvel fans have imagined what would happen if the Avengers finally shared the screen with the legendary X-Men. Now, that possibility is becoming one of the biggest attractions of <strong>Avengers: Doomsday</strong>.
</p>

<p>
Marvel Studios is bringing together characters from different generations of superhero movies, creating a massive multiverse story that could change the future of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.
</p>

<p>
And this is not just another superhero reunion.
</p>

<p>
With Magneto, Professor X, Cyclops and several other familiar mutant characters returning, fans are beginning to ask whether the X-Men will fight alongside the Avengers or become their most dangerous opponents.
</p>

<p>
The excitement has grown even further because of the success of <strong>Deadpool & Wolverine</strong>, which brought renewed attention to the Fox-era Marvel universe.
</p>

<p>
But there is an even bigger mystery circulating among fans: could Tobey Maguire's Spider-Man become part of the same multiverse conflict?
</p>


<h2>
The X-Men Are Officially Returning in Avengers: Doomsday
</h2>

<p>
This is the biggest reason Marvel fans are paying attention.
</p>

<p>
Disney's official cast announcement includes several actors associated with the original X-Men movie universe.
</p>

<p>
The returning actors include Patrick Stewart, Ian McKellen, James Marsden, Rebecca Romijn, Alan Cumming and Kelsey Grammer.
</p>

<p>
Their return connects the original mutant movie era to Marvel's new multiverse storyline.
</p>

<div class="cast-grid">

<div class="cast">
<strong>Patrick Stewart</strong>
Professor Charles Xavier
<small>Founder and leader of the X-Men</small>
</div>

<div class="cast">
<strong>Ian McKellen</strong>
Magneto
<small>One of the most powerful mutants</small>
</div>

<div class="cast">
<strong>James Marsden</strong>
Cyclops
<small>The X-Men's tactical leader</small>
</div>

<div class="cast">
<strong>Rebecca Romijn</strong>
Mystique
<small>A mutant with shapeshifting abilities</small>
</div>

<div class="cast">
<strong>Alan Cumming</strong>
Nightcrawler
<small>The teleporting mutant</small>
</div>

<div class="cast">
<strong>Kelsey Grammer</strong>
Beast
<small>The brilliant mutant scientist</small>
</div>

<div class="cast">
<strong>Channing Tatum</strong>
Gambit
<small>The card-throwing mutant hero</small>
</div>

</div>

<p>
This lineup is particularly exciting because it brings back actors who helped establish the X-Men as one of the most popular superhero franchises in movie history.
</p>

<p>
For longtime fans, seeing these characters return in a major Avengers movie is already a huge moment.
</p>


<h2>
Why Are the X-Men Joining the Avengers?
</h2>

<p>
This is perhaps the biggest question surrounding the upcoming movie.
</p>

<p>
Marvel has revealed that heroes from three distinct universes will be placed on a dangerous collision course as they face an existential threat.
</p>

<p>
That setup creates an opportunity for characters from different Marvel worlds to encounter one another.
</p>

<p>
However, Marvel has not revealed every detail about how the teams will interact.
</p>

<div class="highlight">

<h3>
Two Teams. One Massive Multiverse Conflict.
</h3>

<p>
Imagine Captain America standing alongside Cyclops, Thor fighting beside Beast, and Magneto entering a battlefield where Doctor Doom threatens the future of multiple realities.
</p>

<p>
It could become one of the biggest superhero team-ups ever shown on the big screen.
</p>

</div>

<p>
But there is another possibility.
</p>

<p>
The Avengers and X-Men might not immediately trust one another. If their universes are colliding, they could initially see each other as threats rather than allies.
</p>

<p>
That would create an entirely different kind of Avengers story, where heroes are forced to decide who deserves their trust before facing an even greater enemy.
</p>


<h2>
Cyclops Could Become One of the Biggest Highlights
</h2>

<p>
One of the most exciting returning characters is Cyclops, played by James Marsden.
</p>

<p>
Scott Summers is one of the X-Men's most recognizable leaders. His optic blasts make him an extremely powerful fighter, while his tactical abilities make him essential to the team.
</p>

<p>
For many years, Wolverine received much of the attention in the X-Men movies. Now, fans are eager to see whether Cyclops could finally receive a much bigger moment in a major Marvel crossover.
</p>

<p>
Imagine Cyclops using his full power against an enormous threat while leading the mutants into battle.
</p>

<p>
Could he become one of the most important leaders in the fight against Doctor Doom?
</p>


<h2>
Wolverine: The Missing Piece Fans Want to See
</h2>

<p>
Whenever the X-Men return, one name immediately comes to mind: <strong>Wolverine</strong>.
</p>

<p>
Hugh Jackman's portrayal of Logan has become one of the most recognizable superhero performances in modern cinema.
</p>

<p>
His appearance in <em>Deadpool & Wolverine</em> reminded audiences just how popular the character remains.
</p>

<p>
Naturally, fans want to know whether Wolverine will also appear in <em>Avengers: Doomsday</em>.
</p>

<p>
However, Hugh Jackman's Wolverine has not been included in the published official Doomsday cast list as of this article's update.
</p>

<p>
That means his involvement should still be treated as unconfirmed.
</p>

<p>
Even so, the possibility of Wolverine sharing a battlefield with Thor, Captain America, Magneto and Doctor Doom is enough to generate enormous excitement.
</p>


<h2>
Deadpool and the X-Men Connection: Could Ryan Reynolds Return?
</h2>

<p>
The success of <strong>Deadpool & Wolverine</strong> brought renewed attention to the Fox-era Marvel characters.
</p>

<p>
Deadpool became an important connection between different Marvel movie generations, while Gambit's return gave fans another reason to look forward to the future of the X-Men.
</p>

<p>
Channing Tatum is confirmed in the Avengers: Doomsday cast as Gambit.
</p>

<p>
But what about Ryan Reynolds?
</p>

<p>
At the moment, Ryan Reynolds as Deadpool has not been officially confirmed in the published Doomsday cast.
</p>

<p>
That has not stopped fans from discussing the possibility of Deadpool becoming involved in the multiverse conflict.
</p>

<div class="highlight">

<h3>
Could Deadpool Change Everything?
</h3>

<p>
Imagine Deadpool entering a battle involving the Avengers, X-Men and Doctor Doom.
</p>

<p>
His unpredictable personality could create some of the most entertaining moments in the entire movie.
</p>

<p>
But until Marvel announces his involvement, this remains a fan theory rather than confirmed information.
</p>

</div>


<h2>
Could the X-Men Enter Tobey Maguire's Spider-Man Universe?
</h2>

<p>
Now this is where the story becomes even more interesting.
</p>

<p>
One of the most discussed fan theories surrounding <em>Avengers: Doomsday</em> involves the possibility of the X-Men crossing paths with Tobey Maguire's Spider-Man.
</p>

<p>
Tobey Maguire's version of Peter Parker represents one of the most iconic generations of Marvel superhero movies.
</p>

<p>
Meanwhile, the original X-Men films introduced audiences to characters such as Wolverine, Magneto, Professor X and Cyclops.
</p>

<p>
Both franchises belong to different eras of Marvel's live-action history.
</p>

<p>
The multiverse concept creates an opportunity for these worlds to collide.
</p>

<p>
Imagine Tobey Maguire's Spider-Man suddenly finding himself in a world controlled by powerful mutants. What would happen if he encountered Magneto? Would Professor X see him as an ally? And could Spider-Man become involved in a conflict between the X-Men and the Avengers?
</p>

<p>
These are fascinating possibilities, but there is currently no official confirmation that Tobey Maguire will appear in the movie or that the X-Men will enter his specific universe.
</p>

<p>
For now, this remains one of the most interesting fan theories surrounding the film.
</p>


